  "problem": "In a toy store, a total of $80$ green and red marbles are distributed between three boxes, $A,B,$ and $C.$ Box $A$ contains $16$ red marbles, while box $B$ contains $14$ red marbles. If $50%$ of all the marbles are red, what is the probability that a marble chosen at random is a red marble from box $C?$",
